WEBVTT

1
00:00:04.400 --> 00:00:05.963
Every city has a river.

2
00:00:06.013 --> 00:00:07.715
Coimbra has the Mondego —

3
00:00:07.765 --> 00:00:11.922
and a hill it has been climbing for two thousand years.

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.913
The Romans called it Aeminium.

5
00:00:19.963 --> 00:00:28.508
On the summit they laid out a forum, raised on vaulted galleries that still stand today, beneath the Machado de Castro Museum.

6
00:00:29.900 --> 00:00:36.163
When the bishops moved here from nearby Conímbriga, they brought the old city's name with them.

7
00:00:41.200 --> 00:00:45.826
In 1131, Afonso Henriques brought his court to Coimbra.

8
00:00:45.876 --> 00:00:49.322
From here, a county became a kingdom.

9
00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:54.503
For more than a century this was Portugal's capital —

10
00:00:54.553 --> 00:00:59.333
and its first two kings still lie in the Monastery of Santa Cruz.

11
00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:08.537
Coimbra also keeps Portugal's saddest love story.

12
00:01:08.587 --> 00:01:13.989
Inês de Castro was killed here in 1355, on the orders of the king —

13
00:01:14.039 --> 00:01:15.885
her lover's father.

14
00:01:17.400 --> 00:01:22.536
Legend says the spring where she died still runs with her tears.

15
00:01:24.000 --> 00:01:28.378
Today, a footbridge named for Pedro and Inês crosses the river.

16
00:01:28.428 --> 00:01:32.945
Its two halves meet in the middle — but never quite line up.

17
00:01:35.000 --> 00:01:43.086
Founded in 1290, the university wandered between Lisbon and Coimbra until 1537, when it came here to stay —

18
00:01:43.136 --> 00:01:46.782
in the royal palace, at the top of the hill.

19
00:01:48.600 --> 00:01:51.776
Its tower rings a bell the students call the goat.

20
00:01:56.400 --> 00:01:59.080
Its baroque library glows with gold.

21
00:01:59.130 --> 00:02:06.937
And after dark, a colony of bats patrols the shelves, hunting the insects that would eat the books.

22
00:02:08.400 --> 00:02:15.144
In 2013, the University, the Alta and Sofia became World Heritage.

23
00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:23.879
Every May, students who are finishing their degrees burn the ribbons of their faculties.

24
00:02:23.929 --> 00:02:27.193
The city fills with black capes, and colour.

25
00:02:29.600 --> 00:02:36.854
At night, on the steps of the Old Cathedral, they sing Coimbra's own fado, to the Portuguese guitar.

26
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:41.973
When the song ends, nobody claps.

27
00:02:44.400 --> 00:02:46.059
They clear their throats.

28
00:02:48.000 --> 00:02:50.267
Two thousand years on the same hill.

29
00:02:50.317 --> 00:02:53.384
Every autumn, someone new begins the climb.
